      "cooked": "<p>I’m configuring taxation for an item in ERPNext, where pricing depends on different pricing levels.</p>\n<p><div class=\"lightbox-wrapper\"><a class=\"lightbox\" href=\"https://discuss.frappe.io/uploads/default/original/3X/b/d/bdeea2195f2061d77efeb4a14c7a5589c17ce924.png\" data-download-href=\"https://discuss.frappe.io/uploads/default/bdeea2195f2061d77efeb4a14c7a5589c17ce924\" title=\"Screenshot from 2025-09-05 17-02-00\"><img src=\"https://discuss.frappe.io/uploads/default/optimized/3X/b/d/bdeea2195f2061d77efeb4a14c7a5589c17ce924_2_690x136.png\" alt=\"Screenshot from 2025-09-05 17-02-00\" data-base62-sha1=\"r6dvH0d5R3gBcnaBAeLTSPrggS0\" width=\"690\" height=\"136\" srcset=\"https://discuss.frappe.io/uploads/default/optimized/3X/b/d/bdeea2195f2061d77efeb4a14c7a5589c17ce924_2_690x136.png, https://discuss.frappe.io/uploads/default/original/3X/b/d/bdeea2195f2061d77efeb4a14c7a5589c17ce924.png 1.5x, https://discuss.frappe.io/uploads/default/original/3X/b/d/bdeea2195f2061d77efeb4a14c7a5589c17ce924.png 2x\" data-dominant-color=\"EAEAEA\"><div class=\"meta\"><svg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-far-image svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><use href=\"#far-image\"></use></svg><span class=\"filename\">Screenshot from 2025-09-05 17-02-00</span><span class=\"informations\">778×154 13.6 KB</span><svg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-discourse-expand svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><use href=\"#discourse-expand\"></use></svg></div></a></div></p>\n<p><strong>Challenge:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>GST (28%) must be calculated on the Selling Price (changes by price level).</li>\n<li>CESS (32%) must be calculated on the MRP (fixed at 800 for all).</li>\n<li>ERPNext’s Sales Taxes and Charges Template normally applies all taxes on the same base, but here GST and CESS depend on different bases.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Question:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Has anyone implemented a similar <strong>dual tax base structure</strong> successfully in ERPNext?</li>\n</ul>",
